comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T22:10:10.109Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict 3130-item all-status corpus and live warning/JSON stderr searches found completed related output-format and recurrence work but no exact active owner for this observed Windows failure. Intake only, open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-26T22:10:48.773Z","harness:codex",The current continuation independently read the complete hosted failure log and linked the source alert. A later local Linux full-suite run passes the existing handler-error test; that does not establish the native Windows warning producer or a fix. Reproduction and native hosted proof remain necessary. No implementation claim is taken.
  "2026-10-29T08:28:16.039Z","harness:codex","Nightly run 40837931196 at 2016f0e6870b4631bf2e0f4bfb0fbe983556c3ea reproduces the existing Windows shard 3/4 warning:se prefix before the extension handler JSON refusal; exit status remains 1. Investigating the actual producer and retaining full synthetic-fixture stderr in the next native run before attributing cause. Required PR checks otherwise passed except the separately corrected tracker expected-result gate."
  "2026-10-29T08:31:54.598Z","harness:codex","Added an assertion message containing complete synthetic-fixture stderr before JSON parsing. The test still requires exactly one JSON envelope, command_failed, exit1 and handler-boom; this is diagnostic evidence only, not a claimed fix. No warning producer has yet been established from the native log."
  "2026-10-29T09:02:56.608Z","harness:codex","A real CLI negative control now reproduces the framing failure deterministically on Linux: pass a synthetic Windows home file path to the same throwing extension handler. The native-path control passes; windows-home emits warning:secret_guard_detected:1:rules=absolute_home_path followed by the otherwise correct command_failed envelope and exit1. The public SDK evaluateMutationGuard independently returns that same advisory for the path. Implementing invocation-scoped deferred preflight warnings so JSON failures keep one envelope with warnings and handler detail, while successful invocations retain a structured warning diagnostic."
  "2026-10-29T09:16:24.646Z","harness:codex","The completed focused CLI cohort passes254 tests across four files, including the deterministic Windows-home refusal and a successful guarded mutation. Deferred warnings retain stable codes plus additional remediation text in warning_details, preserve existing diagnostics, and remain isolated across nested/concurrent invocations. Typecheck ESLint and docstring checks pass. The first local full run exposed two test expectation issues (nested create item ID and retaining settings remediation); both were corrected without weakening behavior."
  "2026-10-29T09:17:26.302Z","harness:codex","Native provenance is now confirmed: completed Windows Node24 shard3/4 job123349964084 in run40844923634 exposes warning:secret_guard_detected:1:rules=absolute_home_path before the JSON command_failed refusal on both attempts. This matches the deterministic Windows-home negative control exactly; no settings-read or Sentry cause is inferred. The guarded path is a synthetic fixture under the Windows runner home. The pending revised native run must prove the complete cohort with the transport fix."
